{"zap":{"id":"fb58ff99-fb85-45fd-81dd-32f800f831ce","word":"zap","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"change channels repeatedly","tags":["Brazil"],"word":"zapear"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"change channels repeatedly","tags":["Brazil"],"word":"zapar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"change channels repeatedly","word":"fazer zapping"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["English intransitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive) To make a zap sound."],"glosses":["To make a zap sound."],"tags":["intransitive"],"id":"b6a12a84-3faf-40a2-a893-2ed64558dbb0"},{"links":[["remote control","remote control"],["channel","channel"],["television","television"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"channel surf"},{"word":"channel hop"}],"glosses":["To use a remote control to repeatedly fast-forward or change channels on a television."],"id":"ad8d91e8-7a15-4905-beab-7d2157b6202b"},{"examples":[{"text":"They spent the whole movie zapping bad guys into oblivion.","bold_text_offsets":[[27,34]],"type":"example","id":"06d1f61f-848e-48c8-895b-0eadaa7edf32"}],"links":[["energy","energy"]],"glosses":["To strike (something or someone) with electricity or energy, as by shooting."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"5f6203f5-5ecd-4a0f-8797-cf7164b2aeb4"},{"examples":[{"text":"Says a U. S. officer: \"We zapped the enemy, now we intend to stick around. […]","ref":"1966, U.S. News & World Report, volume 61, page 32:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[26,32]],"id":"e3464999-6836-48aa-9f1b-35c73ce830b9"}],"topics":["government","military","politics","war"],"categories":["American English","English slang","English terms with quotations","English transitive verbs","Quotation templates to be cleaned","en:Military"],"links":[["military","military"],["kill","kill"],["eliminate","eliminate"]],"raw_glosses":["(US, military, slang, transitive) To kill; to eliminate."],"glosses":["To kill; to eliminate."],"tags":["US","slang","transitive"],"id":"51e28956-0e61-4173-977b-6fc7181f6b29"},{"categories":["English slang","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["do away with","do away with"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To do away with something."],"glosses":["To do away with something."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"bfcb147c-c5a5-41a2-8ad2-7bf120e90405"},{"categories":["English slang","English transitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To enliven."],"glosses":["To enliven."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"89ce3611-28f4-4f86-a2a6-6f3a9c4f9fca"},{"categories":["English slang","English transitive verbs"],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To move or transport (something) in a brief time frame."],"glosses":["To move or transport (something) in a brief time frame."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"21cf43df-2738-4b6b-ad03-198a07318156"},{"examples":[{"text":"I think they zapped the processor.","bold_text_offsets":[[13,19]],"type":"example","id":"cd510b77-61bb-417b-b30d-a4f57e29ac65"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["damage","damage"],["electrostatic","electrostatic"],["discharge","discharge"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To damage (especially electronics) with electrostatic discharge."],"glosses":["To damage (especially electronics) with electrostatic discharge."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"e56b37c3-e902-4ba9-baa2-c3095bc08033"},{"examples":[{"text":"If it's not warm in the middle, zap it some more.","bold_text_offsets":[[32,35]],"type":"example","id":"cedba485-d2f9-455b-ba3f-de96eafff6af"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["microwave oven","microwave oven"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To heat (something) in a microwave oven."],"glosses":["To heat (something) in a microwave oven."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"4d8d1bd4-2682-43ce-9f60-24c7d9aa372f"},{"examples":[{"text":"They zapped a lot of files before realizing they had not backed up lately.","bold_text_offsets":[[5,11]],"type":"example","id":"4f8ba443-e778-4700-b4ac-3f6035f5f671"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["delete","delete"],["discard","discard"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To delete or discard (electronic media)."],"glosses":["To delete or discard (electronic media)."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"7f837cdc-a09c-4da9-8a34-0178944aa6a8"},{"examples":[{"text":"They zapped my motor's magnets.","bold_text_offsets":[[5,11]],"type":"example","id":"32e8d02a-a6ef-4407-98ff-baa4cb58e027"}],"categories":["English slang","English terms with usage examples","English transitive verbs"],"links":[["charge","charge"]],"raw_glosses":["(slang, transitive) To further energize or charge (magnetic material)."],"glosses":["To further energize or charge (magnetic material)."],"tags":["slang","transitive"],"id":"a7d7185f-d107-474f-ad0b-4e17cd2d0376"},{"examples":[{"text":"Got to go and zap this document now.","ref":"2004 October 19, Kevin & Lily Shepherdson, “Digital Life”, in The Straits Times, Singapore, page 16:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[14,17]],"id":"95232a4e-1e31-4fec-afff-7fe4fdfdc014"}],"categories":["English informal terms","English terms with quotations","English transitive verbs","Singapore English"],"links":[["photocopy","photocopy"]],"raw_glosses":["(Singapore, informal, transitive) To photocopy."],"glosses":["To photocopy."],"tags":["Singapore","informal","transitive"],"id":"614aa5ca-8299-4252-8403-5aae1c7266f4"},{"examples":[{"text":"We are periodically assailed with appeals to help block this or censor that or zap the other media presentation which one or other of us thinks (often with justice) is injurious to gays or others.","ref":"1976 April 3, 'A. Nolder Gay', “The View From The Closet”, in Gay Community News, page 16:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[79,82]],"id":"4ae406bb-f8f2-49ad-84ed-611bcba4cd95"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["To participate in a zap (protest) against."],"id":"971473e6-8d79-430c-b53c-5b0aaeb5585c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Zaporizhzhia":{"id":"39f88b39-78bd-4c53-9bf7-8d6867070364","word":"Zaporizhzhia","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"city in Ukraine","word":"Zaporíjia"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"city in Ukraine","word":"Zaporozhye"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The Ukrainian government says Kyiv, Vinnytsia, Odesa, Zaporizhzhia and other cities have suffered a barrage of drone attacks, and pleaded with Western countries to step up their assistance in the face of the new challenge.","ref":"2022 October 17, Ivana Kottasová, “‘Kamikaze’ drones are the latest threat for Ukraine. Here’s what we know”, in CNN, archived from the original on 18 Jun 2024:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[54,66]],"id":"f025f15e-98df-4b6d-8b13-3cd53065f727"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Cities in Ukraine","en:Cities in Zaporizhzhia Oblast, Ukraine","en:Hromada capitals of Zaporizhzhia Oblast, Ukraine","en:Oblast capitals of Ukraine","en:Places in Ukraine","en:Places in Zaporizhzhia Oblast, Ukraine","en:Raion capitals of Zaporizhzhia Oblast, Ukraine"],"links":[["industrial","industrial"],["city","city"],["Zaporizhzhia","Zaporizhzhia#English"],["Zaporizhzhia","Zaporizhzhia#English"],["Zaporizhzhia","Zaporizhzhia#English"],["Ukraine","Ukraine#English"],["Dnipro","Dnipro"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"Alexandrovsk"},{"word":"Olexandrivsk"}],"glosses":["An industrial city, the administrative centre of Zaporizhzhia urban hromada, Zaporizhzhia Raion and Zaporizhzhia Oblast, in south-central Ukraine, on the River Dnipro."],"id":"ae9fe7be-df8d-43aa-a866-2c608601a085"},{"categories":["en:Places in Ukraine","en:Places in Zaporizhzhia Oblast, Ukraine","en:Raions of Zaporiz